1
00:00:03,629 --> 00:00:07,048
WELL, THAT THING'S
CLEARLY IN THE WAY.

2
00:00:08,258 --> 00:00:10,177
ALL RIGHT. AHA!

3
00:00:10,218 --> 00:00:12,262
( electrical buzzing)
( screams )

4
00:00:12,304 --> 00:00:14,014
DAMN FRIDGE!

5
00:00:14,055 --> 00:00:16,934
HEY, JOEY, HOW YOU DOING?

6
00:00:16,976 --> 00:00:18,185
GREAT...

7
00:00:18,226 --> 00:00:19,854
ROOMIE.

8
00:00:19,895 --> 00:00:22,690
HUH. YEAH, I GUESS
WE ARE ROOMMATES NOW.

9
00:00:22,731 --> 00:00:24,900
NOW THAT
YOU BRING IT UP

10
00:00:24,942 --> 00:00:26,527
UH, OUR FRIDGE IS BROKEN.

11
00:00:26,568 --> 00:00:28,195
WE HAVE TO GET A NEW ONE.

12
00:00:28,236 --> 00:00:30,739
I CHECKED AROUND AND
YOUR HALF IS $400.

13
00:00:30,781 --> 00:00:32,031
THANKS A LOT, RACH.

14
00:00:32,073 --> 00:00:34,368
I'M NOT PAYING
FOR HALF OF THAT.

15
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:38,288
I'M ONLY STAYING HERE
UNTIL MY APARTMENT GETS FIXED.

16
00:00:38,330 --> 00:00:41,041
LOOK, RACH, MY PARENTS
BOUGHT THIS FRIDGE

17
00:00:41,082 --> 00:00:42,918
JUST AFTER I WAS BORN, OKAY?

18
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:45,671
NOW, I HAVE NEVER
HAD A PROBLEM WITH IT.

19
00:00:45,713 --> 00:00:47,798
THEN YOU SHOW UP
AND IT BREAKS.

20
00:00:49,591 --> 00:00:51,010
WHAT DOES THAT TELL YOU?

21
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:55,806
THAT REFRIGERATORS
DON'T LIVE AS LONG AS PEOPLE.

22
00:00:57,224 --> 00:00:59,267
ALL RIGHT, NOW,
YOU KNOW THAT THE A.T.M.

23
00:00:59,309 --> 00:01:01,436
WILL ONLY LET YOU
TAKE OUT $300 AT A TIME

24
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:03,564
SO I'LL TAKE A CHECK
FOR THE OTHER $100.

25
00:01:03,605 --> 00:01:06,191
YOU'RE JOKING, RIGHT?

26
00:01:06,233 --> 00:01:09,152
OF COURSE I'M JOKING.

27
00:01:09,194 --> 00:01:11,279
I DON'T TAKE CHECKS.

28
00:01:11,321 --> 00:01:14,700
THANK GOD YOU'RE PRETTY.

29
00:01:22,875 --> 00:01:28,129
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

30
00:01:28,171 --> 00:01:30,424
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

31
00:01:30,465 --> 00:01:33,594
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

32
00:01:33,635 --> 00:01:37,723
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

33
00:01:37,765 --> 00:01:40,183
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

34
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:43,395
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

35
00:01:43,437 --> 00:01:46,648
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

36
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:52,613
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

37
00:01:57,826 --> 00:01:58,786
HEY.

38
00:01:58,827 --> 00:01:59,828
HI.
HEY.

39
00:01:59,870 --> 00:02:02,247
DO YOU GUYS KNOW
ANY CUTE GUYS?

40
00:02:02,289 --> 00:02:03,457
WELL, OF COURSE I DO.

41
00:02:03,498 --> 00:02:05,208
MY GOOD FRIEND
JOEY OVER HERE.

42
00:02:08,963 --> 00:02:10,672
OH, I'M SORRY.

43
00:02:10,714 --> 00:02:13,216
THANK YOU, CHANDLER.

44
00:02:13,258 --> 00:02:14,676
ANYWAY...

45
00:02:14,718 --> 00:02:16,386
THERE'S THIS BIG CHARITY BALL
THIS WEEKEND

46
00:02:16,428 --> 00:02:19,098
AND RALPH LAUREN BOUGHT A TABLE,
SO I KIND OF HAVE TO GO.

47
00:02:19,138 --> 00:02:20,140
WHAT'S THE CHARITY?

48
00:02:20,181 --> 00:02:21,600
I DON'T KNOW.

49
00:02:21,642 --> 00:02:26,021
SOMETHING, EITHER TREES,
OR... DISEASE...

50
00:02:26,063 --> 00:02:28,273
RALPH MUMBLES A LOT.

51
00:02:28,315 --> 00:02:30,109
DOES RALPH MUMBLE WHEN
YOU'RE NOT PAYING ATTENTION?

52
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:31,777
YEAH, IT'S WEIRD.

53
00:02:31,819 --> 00:02:35,614
BUT THE THING IS,
I NEED TO FIND A DATE.

54
00:02:35,656 --> 00:02:37,407
WHAT KIND OF GUY
ARE YOU LOOKING FOR?

55
00:02:37,449 --> 00:02:39,534
WELL, SOMEONE
THAT HAS HIS OWN TUX

56
00:02:39,576 --> 00:02:41,453
OR THE ABILITY TO RENT A TUX.

57
00:02:41,495 --> 00:02:44,414
SO HE HAS TO BE A MALE
WHO HAS AT LEAST $50.

58
00:02:44,456 --> 00:02:47,709
OOH, SO CLOSE.

59
00:02:47,751 --> 00:02:48,794
HEY, EVERYBODY.

60
00:02:48,836 --> 00:02:49,878
HI.
HI THERE.

61
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:52,089
THIS IS ELIZABETH.

62
00:02:52,131 --> 00:02:53,132
All:
HI.

63
00:02:53,172 --> 00:02:54,925
I'M THE STUDENT.

64
00:02:54,967 --> 00:02:57,636
OH, ISN'T SHE CUTE?

65
00:02:57,678 --> 00:02:59,013
NO.

66
00:02:59,054 --> 00:03:01,765
YOU KNOW, THIS IS PROBABLY
NONE OF MY BUSINESS

67
00:03:01,807 --> 00:03:05,144
BUT WEREN'T YOU GUYS SUPPOSED TO
NOT BE SEEN IN PUBLIC TOGETHER?

68
00:03:05,184 --> 00:03:06,478
OH, WE'RE NOT TOGETHER.

69
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:07,980
NO, WE'RE JUST TWO PEOPLE

70
00:03:08,022 --> 00:03:09,815
WHO HAPPENED TO HAVE RUN
INTO EACH OTHER

71
00:03:09,857 --> 00:03:11,025
HERE AT THE COFFEE HOUSE.

72
00:03:11,066 --> 00:03:13,485
( giggling )

73
00:03:13,527 --> 00:03:15,320
OH, SLY.

74
00:03:16,864 --> 00:03:19,198
I REALLY WANTED TO
MEET YOU GUYS, BUT
I HAVE TO RUN.

75
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,199
I'LL SEE YOU LATER?

76
00:03:20,241 --> 00:03:21,200
All:
OKAY.

77
00:03:21,242 --> 00:03:22,619
BYE, ROSS.
BYE.

78
00:03:22,661 --> 00:03:24,955
OOPS. DIDN'T MEAN TO RUN
INTO YOU LIKE THAT, SIR.

79
00:03:24,997 --> 00:03:26,999
OH, THAT IS
QUITE ALL RIGHT, MA'AM.

80
00:03:27,041 --> 00:03:29,501
BYE.

81
00:03:29,543 --> 00:03:30,669
SO, WHY IS SHE LEAVING?

82
00:03:30,711 --> 00:03:31,837
IS IT A SCHOOL NIGHT

83
00:03:31,879 --> 00:03:33,463
AND SHE HAS A LOT
OF HOMEWORK TO DO?

84
00:03:33,505 --> 00:03:37,176
YES, HER MOLECULAR EPIDEMIOLOGY
PAPER IS DUE TOMORROW.

85
00:03:37,216 --> 00:03:41,638
OH, TELL HER GOOD LUCK
WITH THAT.

86
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:43,015
ANYONE ELSE? HUH?

87
00:03:43,057 --> 00:03:44,099
BRING 'EM ON.

88
00:03:44,141 --> 00:03:45,851
OH! WHEN'S HER BIRTHDAY?

89
00:03:45,893 --> 00:03:47,769
I DON'T KNOW, RACHEL. WHY?

90
00:03:47,811 --> 00:03:49,688
WELL, YOU KNOW,
IT'S JUST BEEN SO LONG

91
00:03:49,730 --> 00:03:51,523
SINCE I'VE BEEN
TO CHUCK E. CHEESE.

92
00:03:51,565 --> 00:03:53,232
( groans )

93
00:03:53,274 --> 00:03:54,401
OH, I LIKE ELIZABETH.

94
00:03:54,442 --> 00:03:55,485
WELL, THANKS.

95
00:03:55,527 --> 00:03:56,987
YEAH, IN FACT, I
LIKE HER SO MUCH

96
00:03:57,029 --> 00:03:58,780
THAT YOU TELL HER
I WANT MY COOKIES

97
00:03:58,822 --> 00:03:59,781
EARLY THIS YEAR.

98
00:03:59,823 --> 00:04:01,449
YOU KNOW...

99
00:04:01,491 --> 00:04:03,493
A BOX OF THIN
MINTS AND SOME
TAGALONGS.

100
00:04:04,995 --> 00:04:06,371
HEY, COME ON,
GIVE HIM A BREAK.

101
00:04:06,413 --> 00:04:08,289
ROSS, SERIOUSLY,
HOW'S IT GOING WITH HER?

102
00:04:08,331 --> 00:04:10,125
WELL, IT'S ACTUALLY BEEN GREAT.

103
00:04:10,167 --> 00:04:13,253
SHE'S 20, SO SHE'S NOT LOOKING
FOR ANYTHING TOO SERIOUS

104
00:04:13,294 --> 00:04:15,172
WHICH IS PERFECT FOR ME
RIGHT NOW.

105
00:04:15,214 --> 00:04:16,339
WELL, THAT IS GREAT.

106
00:04:16,381 --> 00:04:18,341
AND SERIOUSLY, SHE
SEEMS VERY NICE.

107
00:04:18,383 --> 00:04:20,928
THANKS. I KNOW YOU GUYS LIKE
TO GIVE ME A HARD TIME AND ALL

108
00:04:20,969 --> 00:04:23,138
BUT IT REALLY MEANS A LOT TO ME
THAT YOU LIKE HER.

109
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:24,806
JUST KNOWING THAT YOU GUYS
ARE LIKE...

110
00:04:24,848 --> 00:04:27,308
OKAY, I GOT A GOOD ONE.

111
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:28,476
OKAY, UM...

112
00:04:28,518 --> 00:04:31,521
WHAT IS SHE, LIKE, 12?

113
00:04:41,198 --> 00:04:42,365
CHANDLER, DO YOU THINK

114
00:04:42,407 --> 00:04:44,118
WE TALK ABOUT
OUR RELATIONSHIP ENOUGH?

115
00:04:44,159 --> 00:04:46,120
YEAH.
DO WE HAVE ANY FRUIT ROLL-UPS?

116
00:04:47,871 --> 00:04:48,830
HEY.

117
00:04:48,872 --> 00:04:50,289
HEY.
HEY.

118
00:04:50,331 --> 00:04:52,417
OKAY, I JUST THOUGHT OF
THE PERFECT GUY FOR RACHEL

119
00:04:52,459 --> 00:04:53,877
TO TAKE TO HER THING.

120
00:04:53,919 --> 00:04:55,670
OH, THAT'S SO FUNNY,
BECAUSE WE FOUND SOMEONE, TOO.

121
00:04:55,712 --> 00:04:56,671
OH, THAT'S GOOD.

122
00:04:56,713 --> 00:04:58,173
I GUESS SHE'LL HAVE A CHOICE

123
00:04:58,215 --> 00:04:59,841
BETWEEN MY GUY AND YOUR WEIRDO.

124
00:04:59,883 --> 00:05:02,052
WHY WOULD OUR GUY
BE A WEIRDO?

125
00:05:02,094 --> 00:05:03,678
'CAUSE THAT'S JUST YOUR TASTE.

126
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:05,513
( fake laugh )

127
00:05:05,555 --> 00:05:08,725
SEE, RACHEL'S NOT GOING
TO PICK YOUR STUPID GUY.

128
00:05:08,767 --> 00:05:09,726
OH, YEAH?

129
00:05:09,768 --> 00:05:11,103
YEAH.

130
00:05:11,145 --> 00:05:14,439
MY GUY IS A LAWYER
WHO DOES VOLUNTEER WORK

131
00:05:14,481 --> 00:05:16,608
AND HE HAS ONE OF THESE.

132
00:05:16,650 --> 00:05:18,443
A FACE ASS?

133
00:05:18,485 --> 00:05:21,029
A CHIN DIMPLE.

134
00:05:21,071 --> 00:05:23,573
WELL, UH, YOU KNOW, OUR
GUY WORKS WITH CHANDLER

135
00:05:23,615 --> 00:05:25,200
AND HE'S REALLY
NICE AND SMART

136
00:05:25,242 --> 00:05:26,660
AND HE'S A GREAT DRESSER.

137
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:28,536
HAVE YOU SEEN YOUR GUY'S BODY?

138
00:05:28,578 --> 00:05:31,372
NO. OUR GUY'S
JUST A FLOATING HEAD.

139
00:05:31,414 --> 00:05:33,917
WELL, MY GUY
IS SPECTACULAR, OKAY?

140
00:05:33,959 --> 00:05:35,669
HE'S A MASSAGE CLIENT.

141
00:05:35,710 --> 00:05:38,588
AND ONE TIME,
WHEN HE WAS ON THE TABLE

142
00:05:38,630 --> 00:05:41,424
I LOOKED AT IT,
AND I MEAN ALL OF IT.

143
00:05:41,466 --> 00:05:43,635
YOU'RE NOT SUPPOSED TO LOOK.

144
00:05:43,677 --> 00:05:45,512
OH, YEAH,
LIKE THERE ARE POLICE FOR THAT.

145
00:05:47,014 --> 00:05:48,890
YOU LOOK? YOU-YOU MASSAGE ME.

146
00:05:48,932 --> 00:05:50,058
I KNOW.

147
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:51,559
ALL RIGHT, FINE.

148
00:05:51,601 --> 00:05:54,271
YOUR GUY MAY HAVE
A GREAT BODY

149
00:05:54,313 --> 00:05:56,857
BUT OUR GUY IS
REALLY FUNNY.

150
00:05:56,898 --> 00:05:58,233
CHANDLER FUNNY?

151
00:05:59,776 --> 00:06:00,944
OUR GUY'S A GREAT DANCER.

152
00:06:00,986 --> 00:06:02,237
MY GUY'S WELL-READ.

153
00:06:02,279 --> 00:06:03,530
OUR GUY HAS GREAT HAIR.

154
00:06:03,571 --> 00:06:04,656
MY GUY HAS GREAT TEETH.

155
00:06:04,698 --> 00:06:07,117
OUR GUY SMELLS INCREDIBLE.

156
00:06:07,159 --> 00:06:10,453
DO YOU WANT OUR GUY
TO BE YOUR GUY?

157
00:06:12,873 --> 00:06:13,832
HEY.

158
00:06:13,874 --> 00:06:15,709
UH...

159
00:06:19,504 --> 00:06:20,588
WELL, YOU...

160
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:23,050
YOU DON'T LOOK GOOD, JOE.

161
00:06:23,091 --> 00:06:24,551
WELL, THE FRIDGE BROKE

162
00:06:24,592 --> 00:06:26,469
SO I HAD TO EAT EVERYTHING.

163
00:06:28,096 --> 00:06:30,807
COLD CUTS, ICE CREAM, LIMES...

164
00:06:30,849 --> 00:06:33,810
HEY, WHAT WAS IN THAT BROWN JAR?

165
00:06:33,852 --> 00:06:34,895
THAT'S STILL IN THERE?

166
00:06:34,936 --> 00:06:35,979
NOT ANYMORE.

167
00:06:37,647 --> 00:06:40,483
SO, ANYWAY,
HOW DO YOU WANT TO PAY ME?

168
00:06:40,525 --> 00:06:44,612
IS THIS A SERVICE
YOU'RE PROVIDING ME?

169
00:06:44,654 --> 00:06:47,949
NO, NO, NO...
FOR MY NEW FRIDGE--

170
00:06:47,991 --> 00:06:50,035
OUR NEW FRIDGE.

171
00:06:50,077 --> 00:06:51,370
OUR NEW FRIDGE?

172
00:06:51,410 --> 00:06:53,538
I DON'T LIVE HERE ANYMORE.

173
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:54,915
SO WHAT?

174
00:06:54,956 --> 00:06:56,875
LOOK, OKAY, SUPPOSE WE WERE
A DIVORCED COUPLE.

175
00:06:56,917 --> 00:06:58,210
UH-HUH.

176
00:06:58,252 --> 00:07:00,879
AND I GOT CUSTODY
OF THE KID, RIGHT?

177
00:07:00,921 --> 00:07:05,466
NOW, SUPPOSE THE KID DIES
AND I GOT TO BUY A NEW KID.

178
00:07:08,095 --> 00:07:09,846
OKAY.

179
00:07:09,888 --> 00:07:13,100
GIVE ME $400.

180
00:07:18,605 --> 00:07:20,565
PROFESSOR GELLER?

181
00:07:20,607 --> 00:07:24,194
MM? OH, A STUDENT
I DON'T KNOW.

182
00:07:24,236 --> 00:07:27,697
I WAS WONDERING IF I COULD
TALK TO YOU FOR A MOMENT?

183
00:07:27,739 --> 00:07:28,740
YES, OF COURSE.

184
00:07:28,782 --> 00:07:30,658
WHAT WOULD THIS
BE REGARDING?

185
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:32,452
MAKING OUT IN YOUR OFFICE.

186
00:07:32,493 --> 00:07:33,620
WH-- SHH...

187
00:07:33,661 --> 00:07:35,080
OF-OF COURSE.

188
00:07:35,122 --> 00:07:37,624
WHY DON'T WE GO INSIDE?

189
00:07:39,793 --> 00:07:40,919
( giggles )

190
00:07:44,131 --> 00:07:45,257
MM-MM...

191
00:07:45,299 --> 00:07:46,258
OH, OH...

192
00:07:46,300 --> 00:07:47,550
WHAT?
DOORKNOB.

193
00:07:47,592 --> 00:07:49,177
DOORKNOB.

194
00:07:49,219 --> 00:07:51,263
SORRY.

195
00:07:51,305 --> 00:07:53,390
UM, I ACTUALLY DO
NEED TO TALK TO YOU.

196
00:07:53,432 --> 00:07:54,724
OH, OKAY, WHAT ABOUT?

197
00:07:54,766 --> 00:07:55,725
SPRING VACATION.

198
00:07:55,767 --> 00:07:56,726
SPRING VACATION.

199
00:07:56,768 --> 00:07:58,103
YEAH, WE HAVE TIME OFF

200
00:07:58,145 --> 00:08:00,730
AND A LOT OF PEOPLE ARE
GOING ON TRIPS, AND...

201
00:08:00,772 --> 00:08:02,107
PROFESSOR GELLER?

202
00:08:02,149 --> 00:08:05,277
YES, PROFESSOR FRIE-SEN...
STIN-LINDER.

203
00:08:05,319 --> 00:08:07,362
I'LL BE WITH YOU
IN ONE MOMENT.

204
00:08:09,364 --> 00:08:13,160
SO, I WILL TAKE ONE BOX
OF THE THIN MINTS.

205
00:08:16,163 --> 00:08:17,872
YOU DON'T UNDERSTAND.

206
00:08:17,914 --> 00:08:21,668
ELIZABETH WAS ABOUT TO ASK ME
TO GO ON A TRIP WITH HER.

207
00:08:21,709 --> 00:08:23,420
IS THAT TAKING IT SLOW?

208
00:08:23,462 --> 00:08:24,754
I'M NOT READY
FOR THIS, OKAY?

209
00:08:24,796 --> 00:08:25,797
WHAT DO I TELL HER?

210
00:08:25,839 --> 00:08:26,923
JUST TELL HER THE TRUTH.

211
00:08:26,965 --> 00:08:28,133
TELL HER
YOU'RE NOT READY.

212
00:08:28,175 --> 00:08:30,385
I COULD DO THAT.

213
00:08:30,427 --> 00:08:33,638
WHAT IF SHE GETS UPSET?

214
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:35,598
THEN YOU DISTRACT HER
WITH A BARBIE DOLL.

215
00:08:37,684 --> 00:08:39,644
OR...

216
00:08:39,686 --> 00:08:41,313
YOU COULD JUST, YOU KNOW...

217
00:08:46,776 --> 00:08:48,820
WHAT THE HELL ARE YOU DOING?

218
00:08:48,862 --> 00:08:50,780
WH...

219
00:08:50,822 --> 00:08:52,573
WHAT THE HELL AM I DOING?

220
00:08:52,615 --> 00:08:54,409
YOU JUST BROKE MY FRIDGE!

221
00:08:54,451 --> 00:08:56,661
WHAT? HOW DO YOU KNOW IF...

222
00:08:56,703 --> 00:08:59,831
HOW DO YOU KNOW
IT'S EVEN BROKEN?

223
00:08:59,873 --> 00:09:02,542
OH, YOU THINK I DON'T KNOW
WHAT BREAKS MY FRIDGE?

224
00:09:04,044 --> 00:09:05,212
EXCUSE ME.

225
00:09:06,545 --> 00:09:08,173
WELL, WHAT DO YOU KNOW?

226
00:09:08,215 --> 00:09:10,800
BROKEN.

227
00:09:10,842 --> 00:09:13,011
THAT'LL BE $400.

228
00:09:13,053 --> 00:09:16,348
JOEY, I SAW YOU PUSH HIM.

229
00:09:18,308 --> 00:09:19,434
YOU PUSHED HIM.

230
00:09:21,061 --> 00:09:24,356
JOEY, I DID NOT
BREAK THIS, OKAY?

231
00:09:24,398 --> 00:09:27,775
THAT HAS BEEN BROKEN
FOR A WHILE.

232
00:09:29,903 --> 00:09:32,197
CHANDLER, REMEMBER I TOLD YOU
ABOUT OUR FRIDGE?

233
00:09:32,239 --> 00:09:33,198
UH-HUH.

234
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:34,199
I STILL HAVEN'T GOTTEN

235
00:09:34,241 --> 00:09:36,243
THE CHECK FOR
YOUR HALF YET.

236
00:09:36,284 --> 00:09:37,869
DO NOT GIVE
HIM ANY MONEY.

237
00:09:37,911 --> 00:09:39,413
I'M NOT TALKING TO YOU!

238
00:09:39,454 --> 00:09:41,081
YOU BROKE MY FRIDGE!

239
00:09:49,630 --> 00:09:52,175
YOU WANTED TO SEE ME,
PROFESSOR GELLER?

240
00:09:52,217 --> 00:09:53,927
YES. YES, PLEASE COME IN.

241
00:09:57,556 --> 00:09:58,723
OOH-OOH...

242
00:09:58,765 --> 00:09:59,849
DOORKNOB?

243
00:09:59,891 --> 00:10:02,227
YEAH, IT KIND OF
GROWS ON YOU.

244
00:10:02,269 --> 00:10:03,520
( chuckling )

245
00:10:03,562 --> 00:10:05,480
ACTUALLY, I WANTED TO FINISH
TALKING TO YOU

246
00:10:05,522 --> 00:10:06,814
ABOUT SPRING VACATION.

247
00:10:06,856 --> 00:10:08,191
OH, GOOD.

248
00:10:10,110 --> 00:10:11,778
LOOK, I...

249
00:10:17,033 --> 00:10:19,744
LOOK, I'M HAVING A GREAT TIME
WITH YOU

250
00:10:19,786 --> 00:10:22,789
AND I JUST DON'T WANT US
TO MOVE TOO FAST

251
00:10:22,830 --> 00:10:25,166
OR PUT TOO MUCH PRESSURE ON US.

252
00:10:25,208 --> 00:10:26,709
SO, I'M SORRY.

253
00:10:26,751 --> 00:10:29,170
I JUST DON'T THINK
WE SHOULD GO AWAY TOGETHER YET.

254
00:10:29,212 --> 00:10:30,505
IT'S TOO SOON.

255
00:10:30,547 --> 00:10:32,424
UM, ROSS, I THINK YOU
MISUNDERSTOOD

256
00:10:32,466 --> 00:10:33,632
WHAT I WAS SAYING.

257
00:10:33,674 --> 00:10:35,343
I JUST WANTED TO TELL YOU

258
00:10:35,385 --> 00:10:38,346
THAT I'M GOING TO FLORIDA
FOR A COUPLE OF WEEKS.

259
00:10:42,016 --> 00:10:48,106
NO. I THINK YOU MISUNDERSTOOD
WHAT I WAS SAYING.

260
00:10:48,148 --> 00:10:50,525
WHAT I MEANT WAS...

261
00:10:50,567 --> 00:10:52,068
YOU ARE SO ADORABLE.

262
00:10:52,110 --> 00:10:55,113
THAT... LET'S TALK ABOUT THAT.

263
00:10:55,155 --> 00:10:56,615
( giggles )

264
00:10:58,074 --> 00:10:59,075
HI.
HEY.

265
00:10:59,117 --> 00:11:01,119
HOW DID IT GO
WITH ELIZABETH?

266
00:11:01,161 --> 00:11:02,370
OH, OH, IT WAS FINE.

267
00:11:02,412 --> 00:11:04,247
UH, IT WAS JUST
A MISUNDERSTANDING.

268
00:11:04,289 --> 00:11:06,166
SHE DIDN'T WANT ME
TO GO WITH HER.

269
00:11:06,207 --> 00:11:07,917
SHE JUST WANTED TO LET ME KNOW

270
00:11:07,959 --> 00:11:10,670
THAT SHE'S GOING TO FLORIDA
FOR SPRING VACATION.

271
00:11:10,711 --> 00:11:11,670
WAIT A MINUTE.

272
00:11:11,712 --> 00:11:13,089
IS SHE GOING FOR SPRING VACATION

273
00:11:13,131 --> 00:11:15,008
OR IS SHE GOING FOR
SPRING BREAK? WHOO-HOO!

274
00:11:15,049 --> 00:11:17,885
WHAT'S-WHAT'S THE DIFFERENCE?

275
00:11:17,927 --> 00:11:19,304
WELL, A SPRING VACATION

276
00:11:19,346 --> 00:11:22,056
YOU'RE DOING NICE THINGS
WITH YOUR GRANDPARENTS.

277
00:11:22,098 --> 00:11:24,267
SPRING BREAK,
YOU'RE DOING FRAT GUYS.

278
00:11:25,435 --> 00:11:26,645
HEY, YOU KNOW WHAT?

279
00:11:26,685 --> 00:11:28,855
NOT ALL SPRING BREAKS
ARE LIKE THAT.

280
00:11:28,896 --> 00:11:29,897
WHAT'D YOU DO ON YOURS?

281
00:11:29,939 --> 00:11:32,025
I WENT TO EGYPT WITH MY DAD.

282
00:11:33,776 --> 00:11:35,445
I CAN SEE IT NOW.

283
00:11:35,487 --> 00:11:37,947
LOOK, DAD, IT'S THE SPHINX.

284
00:11:37,989 --> 00:11:39,407
WHOO-WHOO!

285
00:11:39,449 --> 00:11:41,618
I THINK ELIZABETH
IS A LITTLE MORE SERIOUS

286
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:43,620
THAN SPRING BREAK... WHOO-HOO!

287
00:11:43,662 --> 00:11:45,455
ALL RIGHT, I MEAN, COME ON.

288
00:11:45,497 --> 00:11:46,914
SHE'S TAKING MY CLASS.

289
00:11:46,956 --> 00:11:48,208
AND SLEPT
WITH THE PROFESSOR.

290
00:11:48,249 --> 00:11:49,167
I'M GOING TO CALL HER.

291
00:11:49,209 --> 00:11:50,751
YEAH.

292
00:11:53,338 --> 00:11:54,755
HEY.

293
00:11:54,797 --> 00:11:56,633
YOU GUYS, UM, I WANT YOU
TO MEET SEBASTIAN.

294
00:11:56,675 --> 00:11:57,634
HI.

295
00:11:57,676 --> 00:11:59,718
WE JUST MET AT THE NEWSSTAND.

296
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:02,138
WE BOTH GRABBED FOR THE LAST
FIELD AND STREAM.

297
00:12:03,848 --> 00:12:06,267
WHAT? I READ THAT.

298
00:12:06,309 --> 00:12:08,811
CAN I GET YOU
A CUP OF COFFEE?

299
00:12:08,853 --> 00:12:10,605
OH, YES, THANK YOU.

300
00:12:12,857 --> 00:12:14,817
RACHEL, WHAT THE HELL IS THIS?

301
00:12:14,859 --> 00:12:16,444
WHAT?

302
00:12:16,486 --> 00:12:18,196
YOU ASKED US TO FIND YOU A GUY

303
00:12:18,238 --> 00:12:20,699
AND THEN YOU COME TRAIPSING
IN HERE WITH A GUY OF YOUR OWN?

304
00:12:20,739 --> 00:12:21,866
YOU FOUND ME A GUY?

305
00:12:21,908 --> 00:12:23,660
YES, WE FOUND YOU
A REALLY CUTE

306
00:12:23,702 --> 00:12:25,786
AND FUNNY GUY
FROM CHANDLER'S WORK.

307
00:12:25,828 --> 00:12:27,830
YEAH, AND I FOUND YOU ONE, TOO

308
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:29,290
WHO IS NOT A WEIRDO.

309
00:12:29,332 --> 00:12:31,167
WELL, YOU KNOW WHAT,
THOUGH, YOU GUYS?

310
00:12:31,209 --> 00:12:32,835
I REALLY APPRECIATE THAT

311
00:12:32,877 --> 00:12:36,297
BUT I'M JUST GOING TO TAKE
SEBASTIAN TO THE CHARITY.

312
00:12:36,339 --> 00:12:37,424
ARE YOU SURE?

313
00:12:37,465 --> 00:12:39,676
BECAUSE OUR GUY
SMELLS INCREDIBLE.

314
00:12:39,718 --> 00:12:42,345
WOULD YOU STOP IT
WITH THAT ALREADY?

315
00:12:42,387 --> 00:12:43,471
HERE YOU GO.

316
00:12:43,513 --> 00:12:45,306
OH, THANK YOU.

317
00:12:45,348 --> 00:12:46,307
SURE.

318
00:12:46,349 --> 00:12:47,434
SO, SEBASTIAN

319
00:12:47,475 --> 00:12:49,269
DO YOU DO ANY VOLUNTEER WORK?

320
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:51,020
UH, NO, NOT REALLY. WHY?

321
00:12:51,062 --> 00:12:53,314
NO REASON; IT'S JUST
I KNOW A SINGLE GUY

322
00:12:53,356 --> 00:12:55,275
WHO DOES CARE
ABOUT OTHER PEOPLE.

323
00:12:56,484 --> 00:12:57,402
ARE YOU FUNNY?

324
00:12:59,153 --> 00:13:00,113
EXCUSE ME?

325
00:13:00,154 --> 00:13:01,948
WHAT ARE YOU GUYS DOING?

326
00:13:01,989 --> 00:13:03,116
ARE YOU FUNNY?

327
00:13:03,157 --> 00:13:04,492
TELL US A JOKE.

328
00:13:04,534 --> 00:13:08,162
LOOK, I JUST WANTED TO
HAVE COFFEE WITH RACHEL.

329
00:13:08,204 --> 00:13:09,914
YEAH, WELL,
SO DO A LOT OF PEOPLE.

330
00:13:09,956 --> 00:13:13,126
ACTUALLY, UH, I
GOT TO GET GOING.

331
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:14,127
OH...

332
00:13:14,168 --> 00:13:15,920
GIVE ME A CALL
SOMETIME.

333
00:13:15,962 --> 00:13:18,172
YOU DIDN'T GIVE ME
YOUR PHONE NUMBER.

334
00:13:18,214 --> 00:13:19,257
OKAY, SEE YOU LATER.

335
00:13:21,426 --> 00:13:23,219
TURNS OUT HE IS
KIND OF FUNNY.

336
00:13:28,849 --> 00:13:30,310
I CANNOT BELIEVE YOU GUYS.

337
00:13:30,351 --> 00:13:31,478
HE WAS REALLY NICE

338
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:34,021
AND HE JUST LEFT
BECAUSE OF YOU.

339
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:35,440
YEAH, BUT, SEBASTIAN?

340
00:13:35,482 --> 00:13:37,233
WHAT IS THAT,
A CAT'S NAME?

341
00:13:37,275 --> 00:13:39,110
Phoebe:
YEAH, YOU KNOW WHAT

342
00:13:39,152 --> 00:13:40,153
I NOTICED, RACHEL?

343
00:13:40,194 --> 00:13:41,738
HE SCARES EASY, YOU KNOW.

344
00:13:41,780 --> 00:13:44,491
IS THAT THE KIND OF GUY
YOU WANT TO TAKE TO A BALL?

345
00:13:44,532 --> 00:13:47,118
"HEY, SEBASTIAN, WOULD YOU
LIKE TO DANCE?"

346
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:48,869
"UH... OKAY, I GOT TO GO."

347
00:13:50,371 --> 00:13:51,498
ALL RIGHT, GUYS,
STOP IT.

348
00:13:51,539 --> 00:13:52,873
RACHEL, WE'RE VERY SORRY.

349
00:13:52,915 --> 00:13:55,001
THAT WAS A VERY INSENSITIVE
THING FOR US TO DO

350
00:13:55,042 --> 00:13:57,253
AND, YOU KNOW WHAT,
LET US MAKE IT UP TO YOU.

351
00:13:57,295 --> 00:13:59,172
WE HAVE TWO REALLY
GREAT GUYS FOR YOU.

352
00:13:59,213 --> 00:14:01,132
Phoebe:
YEAH, WHAT HAVE
YOU GOT TO LOSE?

353
00:14:01,174 --> 00:14:03,802
YOU MIGHT EVEN END UP
WITH SOMEONE REALLY SPECIAL

354
00:14:03,842 --> 00:14:05,094
IF YOU PICK MINE.

355
00:14:06,596 --> 00:14:08,055
ALL RIGHT.

356
00:14:08,097 --> 00:14:09,808
OKAY, SO YOU WILL
MEET OUR GUYS?

357
00:14:09,848 --> 00:14:11,058
YES, I'LL MEET THEM.

358
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:12,977
IT DOESN'T MATTER
WHICH ONE YOU CHOOSE.

359
00:14:13,019 --> 00:14:14,354
IT'S COMPLETELY UP TO YOU.

360
00:14:14,395 --> 00:14:15,480
OUR GUY IS PERFECT...

361
00:14:15,522 --> 00:14:17,106
OR YOU COULD GO OUT
WITH THE GUY

362
00:14:17,148 --> 00:14:19,942
PHOEBE DEEMED NOT GOOD ENOUGH
TO GO OUT WITH HERSELF.

363
00:14:21,736 --> 00:14:23,112
PHOEBE, THERE YOU ARE.

364
00:14:23,154 --> 00:14:24,781
OKAY, YOU BROKE MY FRIDGE.

365
00:14:24,823 --> 00:14:26,157
YOU OWE ME 400 BUCKS.

366
00:14:26,199 --> 00:14:28,409
OKAY, SURE.

367
00:14:28,451 --> 00:14:29,744
REALLY?

368
00:14:29,786 --> 00:14:31,371
YEAH, YEAH.

369
00:14:31,412 --> 00:14:33,289
OOH, TECHNICALLY,
YOU OWE ME $600

370
00:14:33,331 --> 00:14:36,793
FOR SENDING OUT HAPPY THOUGHTS
ON YOUR LAST TEN AUDITIONS.

371
00:14:41,464 --> 00:14:43,466
CALL IT EVEN?

372
00:14:44,551 --> 00:14:45,885
OKAY.

373
00:14:47,387 --> 00:14:49,723
WELL, THERE
YOU ARE.

374
00:14:49,764 --> 00:14:51,850
SO WHAT DID ELIZABETH SAY?

375
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:54,561
WELL, IT TURNS OUT SHE IS GOING
TO DAYTONA FOR SPRING BREAK...

376
00:14:54,602 --> 00:14:56,020
WHOO-HOO.

377
00:14:56,062 --> 00:14:57,772
THAT MEANS WET T-SHIRT CONTESTS

378
00:14:57,814 --> 00:14:59,858
GUYS DOING SHOTS
OFF OF GIRLS' BODIES

379
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:02,402
WAKING UP NEXT TO PEOPLE
YOU DON'T EVEN KNOW.

380
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:05,405
MAN, SHE IS GOING
TO HAVE A GREAT TIME.

381
00:15:06,781 --> 00:15:09,743
IS SHE STAYING AT
THE HOTEL CORONA?

382
00:15:09,784 --> 00:15:10,869
YOU KNOW THE HOTELS?

383
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:12,161
SURE. I WAS THERE.

384
00:15:12,203 --> 00:15:13,913
SPRING BREAK '81. WHOO!

385
00:15:13,954 --> 00:15:17,041
IN 1981, YOU WERE 13.

386
00:15:17,083 --> 00:15:18,125
SO WHAT?

387
00:15:18,167 --> 00:15:20,002
I DROVE DOWN,
SOLD T-SHIRTS.

388
00:15:20,044 --> 00:15:21,170
HAD A BLAST.

389
00:15:21,212 --> 00:15:23,381
AND YOU KNOW WHO
KNOWS HOW TO PARTY?

390
00:15:23,423 --> 00:15:24,799
DRUNK COLLEGE CHICKS.

391
00:15:26,676 --> 00:15:28,928
OKAY, SHE CAN'T GO.

392
00:15:28,969 --> 00:15:30,638
ROSS, YOU CAN'T TELL HER
NOT TO GO.

393
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:31,930
YOU JUST STARTED DATING.

394
00:15:31,972 --> 00:15:33,307
WHAT AM I SUPPOSED TO DO?

395
00:15:33,349 --> 00:15:35,101
NOTHING. YOU JUST HAVE
TO BE COOL WITH IT.

396
00:15:35,142 --> 00:15:36,603
WELL, WHAT IF
SHE GOES DOWN THERE

397
00:15:36,644 --> 00:15:38,104
AND SLEEPS WITH A BUNCH OF GUYS?

398
00:15:38,145 --> 00:15:40,981
WELL, MAYBE YOU
DON'T MARRY THIS ONE.

399
00:15:47,822 --> 00:15:50,283
I'M SO GLAD YOU'RE
GOING ON THIS TRIP.

400
00:15:50,324 --> 00:15:53,369
YEAH, I'VE BEEN WORKING
SO HARD THIS SEMESTER.

401
00:15:53,411 --> 00:15:55,789
I REALLY NEED TO GO
CRAZY, YOU KNOW?

402
00:15:55,830 --> 00:15:57,123
BLOW OFF SOME STEAM.

403
00:15:57,164 --> 00:15:59,959
SURE, SURE.

404
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,628
LOOK, I DON'T KNOW

405
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:05,172
IF YOUR PLANS ARE
FINALIZED YET, BUT...

406
00:16:05,214 --> 00:16:08,301
HEY, I KNOW ANOTHER GREAT
WAY TO BLOW OFF STEAM.

407
00:16:08,342 --> 00:16:09,218
WHAT?

408
00:16:09,260 --> 00:16:11,429
ARE YOU INTO CRAFTS AT ALL?

409
00:16:12,806 --> 00:16:14,474
ROSS, ARE YOU OKAY?

410
00:16:14,515 --> 00:16:16,643
YEAH, OF COURSE... I'M OKAY.

411
00:16:16,684 --> 00:16:18,978
I'M JUST BEING...
SUPPORTIVE.

412
00:16:19,019 --> 00:16:22,774
SUPPORTIVE OF YOU
AND THIS WHOLE TRIP, AND...

413
00:16:22,816 --> 00:16:25,192
WHAT-WHAT IS... WHAT'S THIS?

414
00:16:26,945 --> 00:16:28,655
IT'S A BATHING SUIT.

415
00:16:28,696 --> 00:16:31,115
TO WEAR IN FRONT OF PEOPLE?

416
00:16:31,157 --> 00:16:33,660
IS THAT SUPPORTIVE?

417
00:16:33,701 --> 00:16:34,993
IS THIS?

418
00:16:37,330 --> 00:16:38,539
HEY.

419
00:16:38,581 --> 00:16:39,998
HEY.

420
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:42,168
WE'RE REALLY GLAD
YOU DECIDED TO
MEET OUR GUY.

421
00:16:42,209 --> 00:16:44,504
YOU'RE GOING
TO LIKE HIM SO MUCH.

422
00:16:44,545 --> 00:16:46,213
WHEN DO YOU WANT
TO MEET HIM?

423
00:16:46,255 --> 00:16:47,423
I DON'T KNOW.

424
00:16:47,465 --> 00:16:49,133
I DON'T WORK LATE
TOMORROW NIGHT.

425
00:16:49,175 --> 00:16:51,636
TOMORROW NIGHT IS GOOD.
TOMORROW NIGHT IS GOOD.

426
00:16:51,678 --> 00:16:52,804
BUT YOU KNOW WHAT?

427
00:16:52,846 --> 00:16:54,514
WHY PUT OFF SOMETHING
TILL TOMORROW

428
00:16:54,555 --> 00:16:55,765
YOU COULD DO RIGHT NOW?

429
00:16:55,807 --> 00:16:56,975
ELDAD, COME HERE.

430
00:16:58,852 --> 00:16:59,853
ELDAD,
THIS IS RACHEL.

431
00:16:59,894 --> 00:17:00,854
HOW ARE YOU?

432
00:17:00,895 --> 00:17:02,313
WELL, A LITTLE BLINDSIDED

433
00:17:02,355 --> 00:17:03,439
BUT, YOU KNOW, GOOD.

434
00:17:03,481 --> 00:17:05,692
ELDAD, SIT DOWN.

435
00:17:05,733 --> 00:17:07,610
MOVE OVER.
MOVE OVER NOW.

436
00:17:07,652 --> 00:17:09,362
THERE YOU GO.
THERE YOU ARE.

437
00:17:11,322 --> 00:17:12,782
OKAY, OKAY,
WE CAN TAKE A HINT.

438
00:17:15,994 --> 00:17:17,370
WHAT ARE YOU
DOING HERE?

439
00:17:17,411 --> 00:17:19,163
THIS IS PATRICK.
HI.

440
00:17:19,205 --> 00:17:20,581
OKAY, YOU'RE
TOO LATE, OKAY

441
00:17:20,623 --> 00:17:22,542
BECAUSE SHE'S
ALREADY WITH OUR GUY.

442
00:17:22,583 --> 00:17:23,793
OH, MY GOD,
YOU'RE RIGHT.

443
00:17:23,835 --> 00:17:25,127
I AM TOO LATE.

444
00:17:25,169 --> 00:17:27,421
THEY'RE SITTING
ON THE COUCH
AND TALKING.

445
00:17:27,463 --> 00:17:28,798
COME ON.

446
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:30,132
RACHEL.

447
00:17:30,174 --> 00:17:31,342
YEAH?

448
00:17:31,384 --> 00:17:32,677
THIS IS PATRICK.

449
00:17:32,719 --> 00:17:34,679
OH, HI.

450
00:17:34,721 --> 00:17:36,806
THIS IS THE GUY
I WAS TELLING YOU ABOUT.

451
00:17:36,848 --> 00:17:39,225
AND BELIEVE ME, THIS SUIT
DOES NOT DO JUSTICE

452
00:17:39,266 --> 00:17:40,601
TO WHAT'S UNDERNEATH IT.

453
00:17:42,020 --> 00:17:43,897
OKAY...

454
00:17:43,938 --> 00:17:45,398
BUT, PHEEBS...

455
00:17:45,439 --> 00:17:47,650
I'M JUST SORT OF IN
THE MIDDLE OF SOMETHING.

456
00:17:47,692 --> 00:17:49,402
OH, OKAY, YEAH,
THAT'S OKAY.

457
00:17:49,443 --> 00:17:50,403
HAVE A SEAT.

458
00:17:50,444 --> 00:17:51,988
YOU CAN'T
DO THAT.

459
00:17:52,030 --> 00:17:53,573
MAYBE I
SHOULD GO.

460
00:17:53,614 --> 00:17:55,867
SIT DOWN.
WE'RE WINNING.

461
00:17:55,909 --> 00:17:57,744
OKAY, YOU KNOW WHAT,
MAYBE I SHOULD GO.

462
00:17:57,785 --> 00:17:59,078
NO! NO!
NO! NO!

463
00:17:59,119 --> 00:18:00,246
YOU HAVE A SEAT.

464
00:18:00,287 --> 00:18:02,248
RACHEL, RACHEL, YOU
HAVEN'T TOUCHED

465
00:18:02,289 --> 00:18:03,249
ELDAD'S HAIR.

466
00:18:03,290 --> 00:18:05,752
IT IS THE SOFTEST HAIR.

467
00:18:05,793 --> 00:18:06,878
I'M GOOD.

468
00:18:06,920 --> 00:18:08,796
RACHEL, PATRICK IS REALLY RICH.

469
00:18:08,838 --> 00:18:10,089
GIVE HER SOME MONEY.

470
00:18:10,130 --> 00:18:11,298
WHAT?

471
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:13,091
UH... YOU KNOW
WHAT, PHOEBE.

472
00:18:13,133 --> 00:18:15,678
THIS ISN'T REALLY WORTH
THE FREE MASSAGE.

473
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:17,847
THAT'S RIGHT, PATRICK.
BYE-BYE.

474
00:18:17,889 --> 00:18:19,974
ELDAD IS MUCH MORE
COOPERATIVE

475
00:18:20,016 --> 00:18:21,267
AND HE CAN DANCE.

476
00:18:21,308 --> 00:18:22,393
YOU DANCE FOR RACHEL.

477
00:18:22,435 --> 00:18:23,477
OH, MY GOD...

478
00:18:23,519 --> 00:18:24,896
NO, NO, NO,
DON'T DANCE FOR ME!

479
00:18:24,938 --> 00:18:25,980
PLEASE, DON'T DANCE.

480
00:18:26,022 --> 00:18:28,232
WHAT IS THE MATTER
WITH YOU GUYS?

481
00:18:28,274 --> 00:18:30,985
YEAH, OKAY, LET'S
TALK IT OUT.

482
00:18:31,027 --> 00:18:33,947
AM I THE ONLY ONE THAT
THIS IS EMBARRASSING FOR?

483
00:18:33,988 --> 00:18:35,031
I'M EMBARRASSED.

484
00:18:35,073 --> 00:18:36,323
SHH, SHH, SHH.

485
00:18:36,365 --> 00:18:37,700
I'LL TELL YOU

486
00:18:37,742 --> 00:18:40,327
WHO SHOULD BE EMBARRASSED--
IT'S YOU GUYS.

487
00:18:40,369 --> 00:18:42,371
COME ON, THIS
IS RIDICULOUS.

488
00:18:42,413 --> 00:18:44,874
THANK YOU, BUT I DO NOT NEED
YOU TO GET ME A DATE.

489
00:18:44,916 --> 00:18:46,125
THEN WHY DID
SHE ASK US...?

490
00:18:46,166 --> 00:18:47,251
I AM STILL TALKING!

491
00:18:47,293 --> 00:18:49,545
AND THEN YOU CHASE
AWAY THE ONE GUY

492
00:18:49,587 --> 00:18:51,171
THAT I ACTUALLY LIKED.

493
00:18:51,213 --> 00:18:53,382
I MEAN, NO OFFENSE
TO YOU GUYS, REALLY.

494
00:18:53,424 --> 00:18:55,885
I MEAN, CONGRATULATIONS
ON... ALL THE CASH.

495
00:18:55,927 --> 00:18:58,387
AND... AND...
YOU KNOW, YOU REALLY

496
00:18:58,429 --> 00:19:00,180
WOW, YOU DO HAVE
VERY SOFT HAIR.

497
00:19:00,222 --> 00:19:03,183
BUT I WOULD MUCH RATHER
GO TO THE BALL ALL BY MYSELF

498
00:19:03,225 --> 00:19:05,144
THAN GO THROUGH
ANY MORE OF THIS.

499
00:19:05,185 --> 00:19:06,437
GOOD-BYE.

500
00:19:08,648 --> 00:19:10,190
NOW, DO YOU USE SOME SORT

501
00:19:10,232 --> 00:19:12,485
OF SPECIAL CONDITIONER
ON THAT HAIR?

502
00:19:12,526 --> 00:19:14,487
YES, PAPAYA EXTRACT.

503
00:19:14,528 --> 00:19:15,863
THANK YOU.

504
00:19:20,451 --> 00:19:23,329
SO, UH, HAVE
A GREAT TIME
DOWN THERE.

505
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:25,123
I WILL.

506
00:19:25,164 --> 00:19:27,125
DID YOU PACK
THAT BATHING SUIT?

507
00:19:27,166 --> 00:19:28,584
YEAH.

508
00:19:28,626 --> 00:19:31,087
IT WAS PRETTY FUNNY WHEN
I HID IT FOR A WHILE, HUH?

509
00:19:34,214 --> 00:19:36,926
ANYWAY, UM...

510
00:19:36,968 --> 00:19:39,762
I AM WORRIED ABOUT
THAT BATHING SUIT.

511
00:19:39,804 --> 00:19:41,722
NOT BECAUSE
IT'S REVEALING

512
00:19:41,764 --> 00:19:43,432
WHICH I'M FINE WITH.

513
00:19:43,474 --> 00:19:46,686
NO, I'M CONCERNED
ABOUT YOUR HEALTH...

514
00:19:46,727 --> 00:19:48,187
UM, SUN EXPOSURE.

515
00:19:48,228 --> 00:19:49,271
OH, DON'T WORRY.

516
00:19:49,313 --> 00:19:50,940
I HAVE PLENTY
OF SUNBLOCK.

517
00:19:50,982 --> 00:19:52,608
IT'S SPF-30.

518
00:19:52,650 --> 00:19:54,485
WELL, IF WHAT'S
IN THE BOTTLE

519
00:19:54,527 --> 00:19:55,528
IS ACTUALLY 30.

520
00:19:55,569 --> 00:19:57,321
I MEAN, SOMETIMES
YOU GET 30

521
00:19:57,363 --> 00:19:58,698
SOMETIMES IT'S FOUR.

522
00:19:58,739 --> 00:19:59,949
AND I SWEAR TO GOD

523
00:19:59,991 --> 00:20:02,242
MORE OFTEN THAN NOT,
IT'S JUST MILK.

524
00:20:02,284 --> 00:20:04,411
ROSS, IT'S GOING
TO BE OKAY.

525
00:20:04,453 --> 00:20:06,372
I'M NOT GOING DOWN THERE

526
00:20:06,413 --> 00:20:08,916
TO HOOK UP WITH
A BUNCH OF GUYS.

527
00:20:08,958 --> 00:20:10,376
I REALLY LIKE YOU.

528
00:20:10,417 --> 00:20:12,252
I LIKE HOW THINGS
ARE GOING BETWEEN US.

529
00:20:12,294 --> 00:20:13,587
REALLY?

530
00:20:13,629 --> 00:20:15,882
YEAH. I'M JUST GOING
DOWN THERE TO RELAX

531
00:20:15,923 --> 00:20:17,550
AND HANG OUT
WITH MY FRIENDS.

532
00:20:17,591 --> 00:20:21,137
OKAY. COOL.

533
00:20:21,179 --> 00:20:22,513
OH, HEY,
HERE THEY ARE.

534
00:20:22,555 --> 00:20:23,973
HEY, ELIZABETH!

535
00:20:25,641 --> 00:20:27,518
( excited shouting )

536
00:20:35,151 --> 00:20:36,986
CALL ME.

537
00:20:42,575 --> 00:20:44,035
RACHEL, WE'RE SORRY
FOR PUSHING

538
00:20:44,077 --> 00:20:45,244
THOSE GUYS ON YOU.

539
00:20:45,285 --> 00:20:46,620
OH, THAT'S ALL RIGHT.

540
00:20:46,662 --> 00:20:47,997
I ENDED UP HAVING
A REALLY GOOD TIME.

541
00:20:48,039 --> 00:20:50,249
THE CHARITY WAS A BIG SUCCESS

542
00:20:50,290 --> 00:20:52,752
AND THEY RAISED A LOT
OF MONEY AND AWARENESS.

543
00:20:52,793 --> 00:20:54,253
SO WHAT WAS IT FOR, ANYWAY?

544
00:20:56,547 --> 00:20:58,549
I WANT TO SAY A DISEASE.

545
00:21:00,593 --> 00:21:01,928
HEY.

546
00:21:01,969 --> 00:21:05,098
I GOT THIS REALLY WEIRD
MESSAGE FROM ROSS.

547
00:21:05,139 --> 00:21:06,432
HE SAID TURN ON MTV.

548
00:21:06,473 --> 00:21:08,601
ALL RIGHT.

549
00:21:11,353 --> 00:21:12,772
OH, MY GOD! LOOK!

550
00:21:12,813 --> 00:21:14,815
THAT'S ELIZABETH!

551
00:21:22,615 --> 00:21:26,326
OH, OH,
PROFESSOR GELLER.

552
00:21:28,454 --> 00:21:30,581
AH, TO BE 13 AGAIN.

553
00:21:30,623 --> 00:21:33,417
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

